{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files -g 'PROGRESS.md' -g 'INTERACTION.md' -g 'STATE.md' -g 'state.json' -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*STATUS*' -g 'adversarial_review.md' . work aristotle_responses | head -100\nfind aristotle_responses/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion-a929306b-83a7dea8-quarantine -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%P\\\\n' 2>/dev/null | head -100\nsha256sum aristotle_responses/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion-a929306b-83a7dea8.tar.gz\nsed -n '1,180p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\nsed -n '1,260p' aristotle_tasks/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion.md\nsed -n '1,240p' reviews/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-closeout.md\nsed -n '1,220p' <original-home>/.codex/adversarial_review.md\"","aggregated_output":"./PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-10f2fe5c-f7631f0b-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p51-_l52ps0z_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P52-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p52-mmt9py1p_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-ae5ca7f3-9cf226e6-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60r-7kr05gwd_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P56-regional-product-state-identity-137c05f7-4b9085b9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p56-4pxeaq7s_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P41-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-7viao_05_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57-sznchb36_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P53-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p53-6si5fpxx_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P50-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p50-n98s99xk_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-665c01eb-43682f4c-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p50u-po2k44mp_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-94c2fd67-fdc0344a-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60-8g_ylnzu_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P50-rerun-d5eadb4d-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p50-81cmr4_p_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P49B-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49b-sn5_fvfw_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations-c0959aa3-7706fefb-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55c-6vvgku8k_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P38-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-0_i1v83l_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P49A-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49a-p0kpdbli_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-b0d05732-e08192b8-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55d-qxitlbh1_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P37-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-y537ze25_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P39-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-oadr2kun_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P40-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-hpzu5w6c_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57a-49mhqqcx_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P49C-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49c-ocehfr10_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55b-r95x55if_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-026bfc92-91db2acf-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p56r-pteblrf2_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P48-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p48-48zqafp9_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P49-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49-gizp5x2z_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\naristotle_responses/P47-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p47-80u8nxnx_aristotle/PROGRESS.md\nc4351cce619e2e7855dc75bbc95621bdc9aa36dbaeda7cafb1fc75728ba0d2fa  aristotle_responses/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion-a929306b-83a7dea8.tar.gz\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-10: P56 is retained as a partial, reviewed artifact. Its\nfinite-word and algebraic direct-limit identities are useful, but its concrete\nextensions depend on `ProductStateBound` and no positivity theorem was proved.\nP56R replaces it as the Lane-H state gate and must derive a genuine unital\npositive C-star functional directly from the finite pure/mixed density-matrix\ndata and the P55D concrete alpha. The original P56 job is disabled rather than\nrewritten, so the distinction remains machine-visible.\n\nIn parallel, P57A ports the *proved* finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite\ntensor pre-Hilbert construction from the compatible Lean-4.28 `bound_beating`\nworkspace into this repository as shared infrastructure. This is a local port,\nnot a cross-project import. Its optional completion/axiom wrapper is explicitly\nexcluded: P57A can establish the algebraic kernel, finite-mode realization,\npositivity, sesquilinearity, and pre-inner-product core, but the completed\nHilbert-space and spatial tensor claims remain P57 work and must be proved\nagainst the local Mathlib API.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-10: P59 is retained only as an audited partial artifact.\nIt restated P57's generic transport but did not construct a `ProductGNSData`\nfrom the P55D/P56R local-hyperbolic model, did not identify that datum's mixed\nGNS representation with P58's `mixedVonNeumann`, and replaced the required\nfactor and trace inputs with fresh premise bundles. The recovery is therefore\nsplit into proof gates: P59A constructs the concrete product datum; P57B\nconstructs the actual Hilbert completion of the P57A vacuum core; P57C proves\nthe pure type-I factor; P59B proves the mixed-UHF bridge; and P59R transports\nthe resulting factorization to the regional algebra. P59T treats traces and\nweights only after P59R, using standard ultraweak normality and an explicit\ninfinite-pure hypothesis for the weight branch.\n# P57B — vacuum-restricted ITP completion\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** complete the proved finite-support vacuum-restricted\n  pre-inner-product core from P57A. This packet makes no manuscript factor or\n  trace claim.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P57B`; Lane `shared`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P57A`, integrated and locally audited.\n- **Gate discharged:** construct an actual quotient/completion Hilbert space\n  with dense algebraic vacuum-tensor image, so later pure-sector work does not\n  rely on an assumed infinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no identification with a pure GNS\n  representation, no `B(K)` closure/factor theorem, no mixed factor, no\n  spatial von Neumann product, and no trace/weight statement.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean`. Starting\nwith `AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedITP.itpCore`, use the pinned Mathlib\npre-inner-product construction to define the seminormed quotient implicit in\nthe core and its uniform-space completion. Prove that the resulting type has\nthe required complete normed complex inner-product/Hilbert structure, that the\nalgebraic vacuum-tensor span maps linearly and isometrically modulo zero into\nit with dense range, and that the vacuum image has norm one.\n\nThe quotient must be genuine: equal zero-norm vectors must be identified by\nthe construction, not retained in a merely seminormed space while calling it a\nHilbert space. Establish every transferred scalar, norm, inner-product, and\ncompletion instance by proof from P57A and Mathlib. If a required Mathlib API\nis absent, expose the exact missing theorem and leave this gate unaccepted;\ndo not introduce a completion structure, quotient, Hilbert instance, or dense\nembedding as a field, axiom, or interface.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nExactly P57A's generic assumptions: `[DecidableEq ι]`, complex inner-product\nspaces `E i`, and unit reference vectors `Ω i`. No definiteness, quotient,\ncompletion, density, GNS, or operator-algebra premise may be added.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean`; import\nP57A and the necessary pinned Mathlib completion modules. Do not import\n`bound_beating`, edit P57A, or use its excluded completion wrappers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion` succeeds.\n- The final completion is an actual complete complex inner-product/Hilbert\n  space, with a proved dense algebraic map and proved vacuum norm one.\n- The module has no `sorry`, `admit`, axiom, opaque completion interface, or\n  claim about GNS/factor/spatial tensor products.\n- The response states how null vectors are quotiented and names every\n  nontrivial Mathlib completion theorem used.\n# P57 closeout review — product GNS tensor factorization\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the packet's stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nRelative to the complete manuscript theorem, this is intentionally **partial**:\nthe module does not prove the pure or mixed factor classifications, factorhood,\nnormal/spatial tensor-product theory beyond its concrete bicommutant definition,\nor the final trace/weight conclusions.\n\nThe exact supervisor-supplied archive\n`aristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9.tar.gz`\nhas SHA-256\n`27aa2166368ee5ded0dc2f5ea2573811bb4b6be623c54f53da69b71a14ecdeed`.  It was\nextracted only into\n`aristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/`.\nNo build, dependency update, or dependency fetch was run in that quarantine\nsnapshot.  Only the packet-authorized candidate\n`AristotleCandidates/ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` was integrated into\nthe live project.  Its live SHA-256 matches the quarantined candidate exactly:\n\n```text\n6e4549050881ec26557bbf243095ae549de03ce6a8628ad4bf4724e2d3478b07\n```\n\nThe archive, quarantine extraction, and this review are retained as raw\nresponse records.  No manuscript file was changed.\n\n## Source and exact scope\n\nThe packet's manuscript source basis is `main.tex:1945-1985`.  Lines\n`1945-1953` state the product-state GNS splitting target\n`\\mathcal H_{\\widetilde\\omega}=\\mathcal K\\otimes\\mathcal K'`; lines\n`1954-1967` contain the later factor/type classification, which is outside P57;\nand lines `1968-1981` describe the separate identification with the regional\nGNS representation and its quasi-equivalence problem.  The candidate therefore\nformalizes the P57 GNS/spatial-identification gate only, not the later\nclassification or source-specific quasi-equivalence theorem.\n\n## Exact assumptions and declarations\n\nThe central declaration is\n`AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensor.ProductGNSData`.  Its explicit fields\nare:\n\n- C-star structures and order structures for `Pure`, `Mixed`, and `Total`;\n- unital star-algebra embeddings `pureEmb : Pure →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total` and\n  `mixedEmb : Mixed →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total`;\n- positive linear functionals `pureState`, `mixedState`, and `totalState`;\n- elementwise commutation of the two embeddings;\n- the product identity\n  `totalState (pureEmb a * mixedEmb b) = pureState a * mixedState b`;\n- the contractivity premise `state_norm_le`; and\n- norm-density of the complex linear span of elementary products,\n  `span_dense`.\n\nThe GNS construction uses positive functionals, so normalized-state fields are\nnot needed for these declarations.  Reading the data specifically as states\nrequires the usual supplied normalization; no normalization is silently used\nto prove a later trace or factor statement.  The algebraic tensor product and\nits completion are constructed in the module.  No completed infinite tensor\nproduct, spatial von Neumann tensor-product API, normal extension, or closure\npremise is supplied as an axiom or interface.\n\nThe load-bearing declarations are:\n\n- `prodElt`, `prodElt_mul`, `prodElt_star_mul`, and\n  `preInner_prodElt`, giving the elementary product algebra and its GNS inner\n  product factorization;\n- `prodCLM`, `inner_prodCLM`, `TensorPre`, `TensorGNS`,\n  `tensorLiftₗ`, `inner_tensorLiftₗ`, and `norm_tensorLiftₗ`, constructing the\n  algebraic tensor map and its isometry;\n- `tensorUnitaryCLM`, `denseRange_tensorUnitaryCLM`,\n  `surjective_tensorUnitaryCLM`, and\n  `productGNSUnitary`, constructing the canonical GNS unitary;\n- `prodCLM_intertwine` and `tensorUnitaryCLM_tensorOpC`, proving the dense\n  finite-word intertwining and its continuous extension;\n- `unitaryConj_tensorOpC`, transporting elementary tensor operators to the\n  total GNS representation;\n- `commute_totalRep_of_commute_prodElt` and\n  `centralizer_representedProductSet`, proving that elementary products and\n  the full represented total algebra have the same commutant;\n- `unitaryConj_image_bicommutant_elementaryTensorSet`, transporting the\n  generated bicommutant through the GNS unitary;\n- `pureFactorSet`, `mixedFactorSet`, `spatialTensorAlgebra`,\n  `tensorOpC_split`, `tensorOpC_commute`, and\n  `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial`; and\n- `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra`, the final concrete equality with\n  `(Set.range totalRep).centralizer.centralizer`.\n\n`spatialTensorAlgebra` is explicitly defined as the bicommutant of the two\ncommuting represented factor families.  This is a project-local concrete set\ndefinition, not an imported standard spatial von Neumann tensor-product\nconstruction.  The candidate documents that pinned Mathlib still lacks the\nstandard tensor-product algebra, commutation, slice-map, and normal-product\nextension API.  The included `trivialProductGNSData` witness only proves that\nthe data structure is non-vacuous; it is not a classification or regional\napplication theorem.\n\n## Acceptance classification\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The conditional product-data theorem constructs the GNS tensor-product unitary, proves the finite-word and continuous intertwining identities, and identifies the represented total bicommutant with the concrete bicommutant-defined spatial algebra. |\n| partial | The result remains generic over `ProductGNSData`; it does not itself instantiate that bundle from the manuscript's regional algebra and P55D/P56R data. Standard spatial von Neumann tensor-product theory and all later factor/type/trace conclusions remain open. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the packet's permitted strongest-local-form gate. The stronger standard spatial-von-Neumann API is unavailable in pinned Mathlib and is explicitly recorded rather than assumed. |\n| failed | None. No compilation, placeholder, archive-integrity, or scope failure was found. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is therefore met at its stated conditional\nscope.  It is not a proof of the complete manuscript claim\n`\\pi_{\\widetilde\\omega}(\\mathcal P_I)''=\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)\\bar\\otimes\\mathcal R`:\nthe classification of the two factors and the source-specific regional\nidentification are downstream work.\n\n## Changed proof route\n\nThe candidate takes a constructive route through the algebraic tensor product\n`PureGNS ⊗[ℂ] MixedGNS`, then completes the norm-preserving tensor lift.  It\nderives boundedness of elementary tensor operators from the proved\nintertwining identity and the isometry, rather than assuming a general\noperator-tensor norm inequality unavailable in the pinned API.  It defines the\nstrongest available concrete spatial object as a bicommutant of the two\ncommuting factor families.  These are alternative proof choices within the\npacket's scope, not silent weakenings; every added premise is a named field of\n`ProductGNSData` above.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P57`; Lane `H`, correct.\n- **Integrated predecessors:** `P54`, `P56R`, and `P57A`, each locally\n  integrated, compiled, and accepted in its closeout review.  The preserved\n  partial `P56` artifact is not used as a predecessor.  The additional GNS and\n  bicommutant imports are already-built local infrastructure.\n- **Permitted gate:** construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space split,\n  prove the dense/continuous intertwining identity, and identify the generated\n  represented algebra with the strongest concrete spatial tensor object\n  supported by pinned Mathlib.  This gate is discharged conditionally on the\n  explicitly declared `ProductGNSData` fields.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The candidate does not claim\n  mixed-factor classification, factorhood of either factor, regional\n  factorhood, `\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)` identification, hyperfiniteness, or any\n  trace/weight dichotomy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization` — passed\n  (`8072/8072` jobs).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct AristotleCandidates.GNSCommutantConjugation AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization Formalization` — passed (`8100` jobs).\n- `lake build` — passed (`0` jobs; live project already up to date).\n- `#print axioms` for `productGNSUnitary`, `prodCLM_intertwine`,\n  `unitaryConj_image_bicommutant_elementaryTensorSet`,\n  `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial`, and\n  `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- A declaration-level scan of the candidate and direct imports found no\n  `axiom`, `sorry`, `admit`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide` declarations.  Textual mentions in explanatory comments\n  were not treated as declarations.\n- `git diff --check` and live/quarantine SHA-256 comparison — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nArtifact types touched: Lean code, mathematical formalization, and workflow\ncloseout metadata.  No acceptance-blocking finding was found.  The review\nchecked that the candidate is the packet-authorized file, that its explicit\nfields account for density and product-state assumptions, that completion and\nspatial objects are constructed at the available scope, that no downstream\nfactor/trace claim is smuggled in, and that no unrelated dirty work was\noverwritten.  Compilation and axiom checks validate the Lean declarations only;\nthey do not validate the manuscript's missing regional coordinate construction,\nnormal/quasi-equivalence argument, or factor classification.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nThe pre-existing modified plan, packet, decision, and queue files, together\nwith all earlier candidates and reviews, were preserved.  The new integrated\ncandidate, exact archive, quarantine extraction, and this closeout review are\nkept intentionally.  The live `.lake/build` cache produced/used by the Lean\nchecks is also retained under the existing project build tree.  No commit,\npush, dependency update, manuscript edit, or archive build was performed.\n# Adversarial Review Protocol\n\nUse this before closing substantive Codex work. The goal is to find defects, not\nto summarize accomplishments.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Identify the artifact types touched: `code`, `math`, `tex`, `computation`,\n   `source-backed`, `workflow`.\n2. Inspect the diff or new artifact against the user's request.\n3. Report findings by severity first. If there are no findings, say so and state\n   the remaining risk.\n\n## Universal Checks\n\n- Did the work answer the actual latest user request?\n- Did it modify unrelated files or broaden scope?\n- Did it overwrite, reformat, or revert pre-existing user changes?\n- Are generated files, caches, logs, plots, PDFs, or build artifacts handled\n  intentionally?\n- Are final claims stronger than the evidence supports?\n- Are verification commands actually relevant to the changed artifact?\n\n## Code Checks\n\n- Does the changed behavior match the stated interface and edge cases?\n- Are tests missing for a changed behavior, bug fix, parser, numerical routine,\n  CLI command, or user-facing workflow?\n- Are errors handled where inputs, files, network calls, or external tools can\n  fail?\n- Is there hidden global state, path sensitivity, nondeterminism, race risk, or\n  stale cache behavior?\n- Did dependency, config, or environment changes alter unrelated workflows?\n\n## Math Checks\n\n- Are all assumptions, domains, signs, conventions, normalizations, and boundary\n  conditions stated before use?\n- Are definitions used consistently throughout the derivation?\n- Is any implication actually reversible, or was a one-way statement used both\n  ways?\n- Are there division-by-zero, invertibility, regularity, convergence, branch-cut,\n  gauge, or boundary-term assumptions?\n- Do limiting cases, dimensions/units, symmetries, and known special cases agree?\n- Are symbolic substitutions justified rather than smuggling in the result?\n- Are claims labeled correctly as proof, derivation, check, conjecture, or\n  numerical evidence?\n\n## TeX And Source-Backed Checks\n\n- Does the document compile if compilation was expected?\n- Are labels, references, citations, bibliography entries, and figure paths valid?\n- Are source-backed claims tied to exact locators when required?\n- Is quoted or paraphrased material clearly separated from the agent's synthesis?\n- Does the exposition define terms before using them in load-bearing statements?\n\n## Computation Checks\n\n- Is the computation reproducible from a recorded command?\n- Are inputs, random seeds, versions, tolerances, and units documented when they\n  affect the result?\n- Are outputs interpreted correctly and not over-promoted beyond the computation?\n- Were independent sanity checks used where feasible: small cases, limiting\n  cases, dimensional analysis, symbolic identities, or alternate algorithms?\n\n## Closeout Template\n\nUse this structure internally, then surface the concise version to the user:\n\n```text\nFindings:\n- [severity] file/path:line - issue and consequence.\n\nChecks run:\n- command -> result.\n\nResidual risk:\n- what was not checked, or why the artifact is not a proof/complete validation.\n\nCleanup:\n- remaining dirty/untracked files and whether they are intentional.\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
