{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"task_root='aristotle_responses/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion-a929306b-83a7dea8-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57b-etkz2bxk_aristotle'\nsed -n '1,240p' \\\"\"'$task_root/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"\nfind \"$task_root\" -maxdepth 2 -type f '\"\\\\( -iname '*response*' -o -iname '*result*' -o -iname '*output*' \\\\) -printf '%P\\\\n'\nwc -l \\\"\"'$task_root/AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean\"\nsed -n '\"'1,320p' \\\"\"'$task_root/AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean\"\nrg -n \"'\"\\\\b(sorry|admit|axiom|opaque|unsafe|implemented_by|native_decide|GNS|Factor|factor|trace|Trace|VonNeumann|completion|Complete|dense|Dense|quotient|Quotient)\\\\b\\\" \\\"\"'$task_root/AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean\"'","aggregated_output":"# Summary of changes for run 83a7dea8-2fe0-4e91-91b2-3e31f5573828\n**P57B — vacuum-restricted ITP completion (infrastructure only; no manuscript, GNS, factor, spatial-tensor, or trace/weight claim).**\n\nCreated exactly one new file, `AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean`, importing P57A (`AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct`) plus pinned Mathlib completion modules. `lake build AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion` succeeds with no warnings; the module contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, or `implemented_by`, and every exported result depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`. P57A was not edited, no excluded completion wrapper was used, and the only assumptions are P57A's generic ones (`[DecidableEq ι]`, complex inner-product spaces `E i`, and the unit reference vectors hypothesis `hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫ = 1`).\n\n**Construction (three proved stages).**\n1. `ITPPre hΩ` — the P57A algebraic span `ITPSpan Ω` (a type synonym, so no structure clashes with `Finsupp`) equipped with the seminormed complex inner-product structure *generated by* P57A's proved core `itpCore hΩ`. Instances: `AddCommGroup`/`Module` transported from `ITPSpan Ω`, `PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ` installed as `itpCore hΩ`, `SeminormedAddCommGroup` from `InnerProductSpace.Core.toSeminormedAddCommGroup`, and `InnerProductSpace ℂ` from `InnerProductSpace.ofCore`. Proved: `ITPPre.inner_eq` (the inner product *is* P57A's `itpInner`), `ITPPre.norm_eq` (`‖x‖ = √(re ⟪x,x⟫)`), and `ITPPre.norm_eq_zero_iff`.\n2. `ITPQuot hΩ := SeparationQuotient (ITPPre hΩ)` — the genuine null-space quotient. Its normed-group and inner-product structures are derived, not assumed (`itpQuotNormedAddCommGroup`, `itpQuotInnerProductSpace`).\n3. `ITPHilbert hΩ := UniformSpace.Completion (ITPQuot hΩ)` — a complete normed complex inner-product space, i.e. an actual Hilbert space: `itpHilbertNormedAddCommGroup`, `itpHilbertInnerProductSpace`, `itpHilbert_completeSpace`.\n\n**How null vectors are quotiented.** They are removed at stage 2, before completing, by the separation quotient of the core-generated seminorm. The null set is proved to be exactly the P57A null space: `mem_nullSubmodule_iff_inner` shows `x ∈ nullSubmodule ℂ (ITPPre hΩ) ↔ itpInner x x = 0`, and `mk_eq_zero_iff_inner` shows `mk x = 0 ↔ itpInner x x = 0` (using `sqrt_re_eq_zero_iff`, proved from P57A positivity `itpInner_nonneg`). Consequently the resulting space is normed (positive definite), not merely seminormed. That the identification is non-trivial is verified concretely: with `ι = ℕ`, `E i = ℂ`, `Ω i = 1`, the theorem `itpEmbed_nullExample_eq_zero` exhibits an explicit **nonzero** algebraic vector mapped to `0`.\n\n**Dense algebraic embedding and vacuum.** `itpEmbed hΩ : ITPSpan Ω →ₗ[ℂ] ITPHilbert hΩ` (from the continuous linear `itpEmbedL`) satisfies `itpEmbed_inner` (preserves P57A's form), `norm_itpEmbed` (isometric for the core seminorm), `itpEmbed_eq_iff` / `itpEmbed_eq_zero_iff` (identifies exactly the null vectors), `denseRange_itpEmbed` (dense algebraic image), and `norm_itpEmbed_vacuumVector : ‖itpEmbed hΩ (vacuumVector Ω)‖ = 1` with `itpEmbed_vacuumVector_ne_zero`.\n\n**Nontrivial Mathlib theorems/instances used:** `InnerProductSpace.Core.toSeminormedAddCommGroup` and `InnerProductSpace.ofCore` (with the Cauchy–Schwarz-based triangle inequality behind them); the `SeparationQuotient` normed-group instance and `SeparationQuotient.norm_mk`, `SeparationQuotient.surjective_mk`, `SeparationQuotient.mkCLM`; the `SeparationQuotient` `InnerProductSpace` instance with `SeparationQuotient.inner_mk_mk` (via `Inseparable.inner_eq_inner`); `UniformSpace.Completion`'s normed-group instance with `UniformSpace.Completion.norm_coe`, its `CompleteSpace` instance, `UniformSpace.Completion.denseRange_coe`, `UniformSpace.Completion.toComplL`, and `UniformSpace.Completion.innerProductSpace` with `UniformSpace.Completion.inner_coe` (whose proof uses the dense-inducing bilinear extension); plus `nullSubmodule`/`mem_nullSubmodule_iff`. No required Mathlib API was missing, so the gate is discharged without any assumed completion structure or interface.\n\nNo downstream claim is made: nothing here identifies the space with a GNS representation, asserts a `B(K)` closure or factorhood, forms a spatial von Neumann tensor product, or mentions traces or weights.321 aristotle_responses/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion-a929306b-83a7dea8-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p57b-etkz2bxk_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean\n/-\nP57B — vacuum-restricted ITP quotient and completion.\n\n**Context declaration: Infrastructure only.**  This file makes no manuscript\nclaim: no GNS identification, no `B(K)` closure or factor theorem, no spatial\nvon Neumann tensor product, and no trace or weight statement.\n\nStarting from the *proved* finite-support pre-inner-product core\n`AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedITP.itpCore` of P57A, this module builds\nthe Hilbert space implicit in that core:\n\n* `ITPPre hΩ` — the algebraic span `ITPSpan Ω` carrying the seminormed\n  complex inner-product structure generated by `itpCore hΩ` (Mathlib's\n  `InnerProductSpace.Core.toSeminormedAddCommGroup` and\n  `InnerProductSpace.ofCore`);\n* `ITPQuot hΩ = SeparationQuotient (ITPPre hΩ)` — the genuine quotient by the\n  null space `{x | ‖x‖ = 0} = {x | ⟪x, x⟫ = 0}`, a *normed* (hence\n  positive-definite) complex inner-product space\n  (`SeparationQuotient`'s `NormedAddCommGroup` instance from\n  `Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Uniform` and its `InnerProductSpace` instance\n  from `Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Completion`);\n* `ITPHilbert hΩ = UniformSpace.Completion (ITPQuot hΩ)` — its uniform-space\n  completion, a complete normed complex inner-product space, i.e. a Hilbert\n  space (`UniformSpace.Completion.instNormedAddCommGroup`, the completion's\n  `CompleteSpace` instance, and\n  `UniformSpace.Completion.innerProductSpace`).\n\nThe algebraic span maps into it by the continuous linear map\n`itpEmbed hΩ : ITPSpan Ω →ₗ[ℂ] ITPHilbert hΩ`, which\n\n* preserves the P57A form: `itpEmbed_inner`;\n* is isometric for the core seminorm: `norm_itpEmbed`;\n* identifies exactly the null vectors: `itpEmbed_eq_iff`,\n  `itpEmbed_eq_zero_iff`;\n* has dense range: `denseRange_itpEmbed`; and\n* sends the algebraic vacuum to a unit vector: `norm_itpEmbed_vacuumVector`.\n\nNothing here is assumed: every instance is transferred by proof from P57A and\nthe pinned Mathlib, and no axiom, `sorry`, or completion interface is used.\n-/\nimport AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Completion\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Module.Completion\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.NullSubmodule\n\nopen scoped ComplexConjugate ComplexOrder InnerProductSpace\n\nset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 1000000\nset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n\nnamespace AristotleCandidates\nnamespace VacuumRestrictedITP\n\nuniverse u v\n\n/-- A nonnegative complex number vanishes iff the square root of its real part does. -/\ntheorem sqrt_re_eq_zero_iff {c : ℂ} (hc : 0 ≤ c) : √(RCLike.re c) = 0 ↔ c = 0 := by\n  obtain ⟨hre, him⟩ := Complex.le_def.mp hc\n  have hre' : (0 : ℝ) ≤ c.re := by simpa using hre\n  constructor\n  · intro h\n    have : c.re = 0 := by\n      have := Real.sq_sqrt (by simpa using hre' : (0:ℝ) ≤ RCLike.re c)\n      rw [h] at this\n      simpa [eq_comm] using this\n    exact Complex.ext (by simpa using this) (by simpa using him.symm)\n  · intro h\n    simp [h]\n\nvariable {ι : Type u} {E : ι → Type v}\n  [∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (E i)] [∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)]\n  {Ω : ∀ i, E i} [DecidableEq ι]\n\n/-! ## The seminormed pre-Hilbert space of the algebraic span -/\n\n/-- The algebraic span of vacuum-restricted elementary tensors, viewed as a type carrying the\nseminormed complex inner-product structure produced by the P57A core `itpCore hΩ`.  This is a\ntype synonym for `ITPSpan Ω`; the synonym exists only so that the core-generated seminorm does\nnot clash with any other structure on `Finsupp`. -/\ndef ITPPre (_hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) : Type max u v := ITPSpan Ω\n\nnamespace ITPPre\n\nvariable (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1)\n\nnoncomputable instance : AddCommGroup (ITPPre hΩ) := inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup (ITPSpan Ω))\n\nnoncomputable instance : Module ℂ (ITPPre hΩ) := inferInstanceAs (Module ℂ (ITPSpan Ω))\n\n/-- The P57A pre-inner-product core, installed as a class instance on the synonym. -/\nnoncomputable instance instCore : PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (ITPPre hΩ) := itpCore hΩ\n\n/-- The seminormed group structure generated by the core. -/\nnoncomputable instance instSeminormedAddCommGroup : SeminormedAddCommGroup (ITPPre hΩ) :=\n  InnerProductSpace.Core.toSeminormedAddCommGroup (𝕜 := ℂ) (F := ITPPre hΩ)\n\n/-- The (semi-definite) complex inner-product space structure generated by the core. -/\nnoncomputable instance instInnerProductSpace : InnerProductSpace ℂ (ITPPre hΩ) :=\n  InnerProductSpace.ofCore (F := ITPPre hΩ) (instCore hΩ)\n\n/-- The inner product on `ITPPre hΩ` is the P57A sesquilinear form. -/\n@[simp] theorem inner_eq (x y : ITPPre hΩ) :\n    ⟪x, y⟫_ℂ = itpInner (Ω := Ω) x y := rfl\n\ntheorem norm_eq (x : ITPPre hΩ) : ‖x‖ = √(RCLike.re (itpInner (Ω := Ω) x x)) := rfl\n\n/-- The seminorm of `x` vanishes exactly when `x` is null for the P57A form. -/\ntheorem norm_eq_zero_iff (x : ITPPre hΩ) : ‖x‖ = 0 ↔ itpInner (Ω := Ω) x x = 0 := by\n  rw [norm_eq]\n  exact sqrt_re_eq_zero_iff (itpInner_nonneg hΩ x)\n\nend ITPPre\n\n/-! ## The null-space quotient -/\n\n/-- The genuine quotient of the algebraic span by its null space: two elements of `ITPPre hΩ`\nbecome equal exactly when their difference has vanishing self-inner-product. -/\nabbrev ITPQuot (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) : Type max u v := SeparationQuotient (ITPPre hΩ)\n\nsection Quot\n\nvariable (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1)\n\n/-- The quotient carries a genuine (positive definite) norm. -/\nnoncomputable def itpQuotNormedAddCommGroup : NormedAddCommGroup (ITPQuot hΩ) := inferInstance\n\n/-- The quotient is a complex inner-product space. -/\nnoncomputable def itpQuotInnerProductSpace : InnerProductSpace ℂ (ITPQuot hΩ) := inferInstance\n\n/-- The null space that is being quotiented out is exactly the set of vectors with vanishing\nself-inner-product for the P57A form. -/\ntheorem mem_nullSubmodule_iff_inner (x : ITPPre hΩ) :\n    x ∈ nullSubmodule ℂ (ITPPre hΩ) ↔ itpInner (Ω := Ω) x x = 0 := by\n  rw [mem_nullSubmodule_iff, ITPPre.norm_eq_zero_iff hΩ]\n\n/-- The quotient map kills exactly the null vectors: this is the null-space quotient. -/\ntheorem mk_eq_zero_iff_inner (x : ITPPre hΩ) :\n    (SeparationQuotient.mk x : ITPQuot hΩ) = 0 ↔ itpInner (Ω := Ω) x x = 0 := by\n  rw [← norm_eq_zero (E := ITPQuot hΩ) (a := SeparationQuotient.mk x),\n    SeparationQuotient.norm_mk, ITPPre.norm_eq_zero_iff hΩ]\n\nend Quot\n\n/-! ## The completion: an actual Hilbert space -/\n\n/-- The vacuum-restricted infinite tensor product Hilbert space: the completion of the\nnull-space quotient of the algebraic span. -/\nabbrev ITPHilbert (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1) : Type max u v :=\n  UniformSpace.Completion (ITPQuot hΩ)\n\nsection Hilbert\n\nvariable (hΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1)\n\n/-- `ITPHilbert hΩ` carries a genuine (positive definite) norm. -/\nnoncomputable def itpHilbertNormedAddCommGroup : NormedAddCommGroup (ITPHilbert hΩ) :=\n  inferInstance\n\n/-- `ITPHilbert hΩ` is a complex inner-product space. -/\nnoncomputable def itpHilbertInnerProductSpace : InnerProductSpace ℂ (ITPHilbert hΩ) :=\n  inferInstance\n\n/-- `ITPHilbert hΩ` is complete: together with the two structures above it is a Hilbert space. -/\ntheorem itpHilbert_completeSpace : CompleteSpace (ITPHilbert hΩ) := inferInstance\n\n/-- The canonical continuous linear map from the algebraic span into the completion. -/\nnoncomputable def itpEmbedL : ITPPre hΩ →L[ℂ] ITPHilbert hΩ :=\n  (UniformSpace.Completion.toComplL : ITPQuot hΩ →L[ℂ] ITPHilbert hΩ).comp\n    (SeparationQuotient.mkCLM ℂ (ITPPre hΩ))\n\n/-- The canonical linear map from the P57A algebraic span into the completion Hilbert space. -/\nnoncomputable def itpEmbed : ITPSpan Ω →ₗ[ℂ] ITPHilbert hΩ := (itpEmbedL hΩ).toLinearMap\n\ntheorem itpEmbed_apply (x : ITPSpan Ω) :\n    itpEmbed hΩ x\n      = ((SeparationQuotient.mk (x : ITPPre hΩ) : ITPQuot hΩ) : ITPHilbert hΩ) := rfl\n\n/-- **The embedding preserves the P57A form.** -/\n@[simp] theorem itpEmbed_inner (x y : ITPSpan Ω) :\n    ⟪itpEmbed hΩ x, itpEmbed hΩ y⟫_ℂ = itpInner (Ω := Ω) x y := by\n  rw [itpEmbed_apply, itpEmbed_apply, UniformSpace.Completion.inner_coe,\n    SeparationQuotient.inner_mk_mk, ITPPre.inner_eq]\n\n/-- **The embedding is isometric for the core seminorm.** -/\ntheorem norm_itpEmbed (x : ITPSpan Ω) :\n    ‖itpEmbed hΩ x‖ = √(RCLike.re (itpInner (Ω := Ω) x x)) := by\n  rw [itpEmbed_apply, UniformSpace.Completion.norm_coe, SeparationQuotient.norm_mk,\n    ITPPre.norm_eq]\n\n/-- **The embedding identifies exactly the null vectors**: two algebraic vectors have the same\nimage iff their difference is null for the P57A form.  This is what makes the construction a\ngenuine quotient rather than a seminormed space renamed as a Hilbert space. -/\ntheorem itpEmbed_eq_iff (x y : ITPSpan Ω) :\n    itpEmbed hΩ x = itpEmbed hΩ y ↔ itpInner (Ω := Ω) (x - y) (x - y) = 0 := by\n  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub, ← norm_eq_zero (a := itpEmbed hΩ (x - y)), norm_itpEmbed]\n  exact sqrt_re_eq_zero_iff (itpInner_nonneg hΩ (x - y))\n\ntheorem itpEmbed_eq_zero_iff (x : ITPSpan Ω) :\n    itpEmbed hΩ x = 0 ↔ itpInner (Ω := Ω) x x = 0 := by\n  rw [← norm_eq_zero (a := itpEmbed hΩ x), norm_itpEmbed]\n  exact sqrt_re_eq_zero_iff (itpInner_nonneg hΩ x)\n\n/-- **The algebraic image is dense.** -/\ntheorem denseRange_itpEmbed : DenseRange (itpEmbed hΩ) := by\n  have hcoe : DenseRange ((↑) : ITPQuot hΩ → ITPHilbert hΩ) :=\n    UniformSpace.Completion.denseRange_coe\n  have hmk : Function.Surjective (SeparationQuotient.mk : ITPPre hΩ → ITPQuot hΩ) :=\n    SeparationQuotient.surjective_mk\n  have hrange : Set.range (itpEmbed hΩ) = Set.range ((↑) : ITPQuot hΩ → ITPHilbert hΩ) := by\n    apply Set.Subset.antisymm\n    · rintro z ⟨x, rfl⟩\n      exact ⟨SeparationQuotient.mk (x : ITPPre hΩ), rfl⟩\n    · rintro z ⟨q, rfl⟩\n      obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hmk q\n      exact ⟨(x : ITPSpan Ω), rfl⟩\n  rw [DenseRange, hrange]\n  exact hcoe\n\n/-- **The vacuum image is a unit vector.** -/\n@[simp] theorem norm_itpEmbed_vacuumVector :\n    ‖itpEmbed hΩ (vacuumVector Ω)‖ = 1 := by\n  rw [norm_itpEmbed, itpInner_vacuumVector]\n  simp\n\n/-- The vacuum image is in particular nonzero, so the completion is nontrivial. -/\ntheorem itpEmbed_vacuumVector_ne_zero : itpEmbed hΩ (vacuumVector Ω) ≠ 0 := by\n  intro h\n  have hn := norm_itpEmbed_vacuumVector hΩ\n  rw [h] at hn\n  simp at hn\n\nend Hilbert\n\n/-! ## The quotient is not vacuous\n\nThe algebraic span really does contain nonzero null vectors, so the passage to\n`SeparationQuotient` genuinely identifies distinct algebraic vectors.  Take `ι = ℕ`, `E i = ℂ`,\n`Ω i = 1`; the elementary tensor which is `1` in every mode but declares mode `0` active is a\ndifferent `VacuumTensor` from the vacuum, yet all four kernels are `1`, so their difference is a\nnonzero null vector. -/\n\nsection Nondegenerate\n\n/-- The all-ones elementary tensor over `ι = ℕ` with mode `0` declared active. -/\ndef dupTensor : VacuumTensor (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ)) where\n  vec _ := 1\n  active := {0}\n  vec_eq_vacuum _ _ := rfl\n\ntheorem vacuum_inner_one : ∀ _i : ℕ, ⟪(1 : ℂ), (1 : ℂ)⟫_ℂ = 1 := by\n  intro _; simp\n\ntheorem dupTensor_ne_vacuum :\n    dupTensor ≠ VacuumTensor.vacuum (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ)) := by\n  intro h\n  have hact : dupTensor.active = (VacuumTensor.vacuum (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ))).active := by rw [h]\n  simp [dupTensor, VacuumTensor.vacuum] at hact\n\n/-- A nonzero vector of the algebraic span which is null for the P57A form. -/\nnoncomputable def nullExample : ITPSpan (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ)) :=\n  Finsupp.single dupTensor 1 - Finsupp.single (VacuumTensor.vacuum (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ))) 1\n\ntheorem nullExample_dup : nullExample dupTensor = 1 := by\n  rw [nullExample, Finsupp.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same,\n    Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne dupTensor_ne_vacuum]\n  ring\n\ntheorem nullExample_vacuum :\n    nullExample (VacuumTensor.vacuum (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ))) = -1 := by\n  rw [nullExample, Finsupp.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same,\n    Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (Ne.symm dupTensor_ne_vacuum)]\n  ring\n\ntheorem nullExample_ne_zero : nullExample ≠ 0 := by\n  intro h\n  have hv : nullExample dupTensor = 0 := by rw [h]; rfl\n  rw [nullExample_dup] at hv\n  exact one_ne_zero hv\n\ntheorem itpInner_nullExample : itpInner nullExample nullExample = 0 := by\n  classical\n  set t : Finset (VacuumTensor (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ))) :=\n    {dupTensor, VacuumTensor.vacuum (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ))} with ht\n  have hsupp : (nullExample).support ⊆ t := by\n    refine (Finsupp.support_sub).trans (Finset.union_subset ?_ ?_)\n    · exact Finsupp.support_single_subset.trans (by simp [ht])\n    · exact Finsupp.support_single_subset.trans (by simp [ht])\n  have hkern : ∀ v ∈ t, ∀ w ∈ t, kern v w = 1 := by\n    intro v hv w hw\n    have hv' : v.vec = fun _ => (1 : ℂ) := by\n      rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hv with h | h\n      · subst h; rfl\n      · rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at h; subst h; rfl\n    have hw' : w.vec = fun _ => (1 : ℂ) := by\n      rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hw with h | h\n      · subst h; rfl\n      · rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at h; subst h; rfl\n    simp [kern, hv', hw']\n  have hsum : ∑ w ∈ t, nullExample w = 0 := by\n    rw [ht, Finset.sum_pair dupTensor_ne_vacuum, nullExample_dup, nullExample_vacuum]\n    ring\n  have hconj : ∑ v ∈ t, (starRingEnd ℂ) (nullExample v) = 0 := by\n    rw [← map_sum, hsum, map_zero]\n  rw [itpInner_eq_sum hsupp hsupp]\n  have hrw : ∀ v ∈ t, ∑ w ∈ t, (starRingEnd ℂ) (nullExample v) * nullExample w * kern v w\n      = ∑ w ∈ t, (starRingEnd ℂ) (nullExample v) * nullExample w := by\n    intro v hv\n    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun w hw => ?_\n    rw [hkern v hv w hw, mul_one]\n  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl hrw, ← Finset.sum_mul_sum, hconj, zero_mul]\n\n/-- **The quotient is genuine**: a nonzero algebraic vector is sent to `0` in the completion. -/\ntheorem itpEmbed_nullExample_eq_zero :\n    itpEmbed (Ω := fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℂ)) vacuum_inner_one nullExample = 0 ∧ nullExample ≠ 0 :=\n  ⟨(itpEmbed_eq_zero_iff vacuum_inner_one nullExample).2 itpInner_nullExample,\n    nullExample_ne_zero⟩\n\nend Nondegenerate\n\nend VacuumRestrictedITP\n2:P57B — vacuum-restricted ITP quotient and completion.\n5:claim: no GNS identification, no `B(K)` closure or factor theorem, no spatial\n6:von Neumann tensor product, and no trace or weight statement.\n16:* `ITPQuot hΩ = SeparationQuotient (ITPPre hΩ)` — the genuine quotient by the\n23:  completion, a complete normed complex inner-product space, i.e. a Hilbert\n24:  space (`UniformSpace.Completion.instNormedAddCommGroup`, the completion's\n35:* has dense range: `denseRange_itpEmbed`; and\n39:the pinned Mathlib, and no axiom, `sorry`, or completion interface is used.\n114:/-! ## The null-space quotient -/\n116:/-- The genuine quotient of the algebraic span by its null space: two elements of `ITPPre hΩ`\n124:/-- The quotient carries a genuine (positive definite) norm. -/\n127:/-- The quotient is a complex inner-product space. -/\n136:/-- The quotient map kills exactly the null vectors: this is the null-space quotient. -/\n144:/-! ## The completion: an actual Hilbert space -/\n146:/-- The vacuum-restricted infinite tensor product Hilbert space: the completion of the\n147:null-space quotient of the algebraic span. -/\n166:/-- The canonical continuous linear map from the algebraic span into the completion. -/\n171:/-- The canonical linear map from the P57A algebraic span into the completion Hilbert space. -/\n192:genuine quotient rather than a seminormed space renamed as a Hilbert space. -/\n203:/-- **The algebraic image is dense.** -/\n225:/-- The vacuum image is in particular nonzero, so the completion is nontrivial. -/\n234:/-! ## The quotient is not vacuous\n312:/-- **The quotient is genuine**: a nonzero algebraic vector is sent to `0` in the completion. -/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
